
  Updates on this box are by hand, from the control node, one host at a time:

    cd ~/infra/ansible
    ansible-playbook playbooks/server-update-leap.yml -e target=HOST -K

  It updates, moves the cloudflared and Compose pins, reboots, and reports done
  once the box answers again.

  The Pi's boot firmware is locked and changes only with someone at the console.
  On the box, in one shell, then watch it come back:

    sudo transactional-update shell
      zypper removelock 'u-boot-rpi*' 'raspberrypi-firmware*' 'raspberrypi-eeprom*'
      zypper update 'u-boot-rpi*' 'raspberrypi-firmware*' 'raspberrypi-eeprom*'
      zypper addlock 'u-boot-rpi*' 'raspberrypi-firmware*' 'raspberrypi-eeprom*'
      exit
    sudo systemctl reboot

